1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,717
Wednesday, 12 March 2025.

2
00:00:01,717 --> 00:00:07,026
Stockholm District Court receives a bankruptcy petition from Northvolt AB and four Swedish subsidiaries.

3
00:00:07,026 --> 00:00:18,784
Around three thousand people at the Skellefteå factory, some on work visas that depend on the job, learn of it in a Teams call about as long as the word "konkurs".

4
00:00:18,784 --> 00:00:21,059
A trustee, Mikael Kubu, is appointed.

5
00:00:21,059 --> 00:00:28,266
Claims will eventually reach about ninety billion kronor, some eight billion dollars, owed to seventeen banks and several governments.

6
00:00:28,266 --> 00:00:33,955
By capital invested, headcount and debt, it is the largest bankruptcy in modern Swedish history.

7
00:00:33,955 --> 00:00:38,127
Eight years earlier, this company had been Europe's answer to China.

8
00:00:38,127 --> 00:00:40,023
This is how it went.

9
00:00:40,423 --> 00:00:45,151
That was the interim chairman on bankruptcy day, and the metaphor deserves a pause.

10
00:00:45,151 --> 00:00:47,177
Northvolt had not run a marathon.

11
00:00:47,177 --> 00:00:54,945
It had raised, by its own count, more than thirteen billion dollars in equity and debt, closer to fifteen with guarantees and commitments.

12
00:00:54,945 --> 00:01:01,700
It had built one of Europe's largest industrial sites, roughly twice the footprint of Arlanda airport, according to the trustee.

13
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:08,116
And in the one year that mattered, it delivered less than half a percent of what it had promised.

14
00:01:08,116 --> 00:01:13,182
To understand how, go back to 2015 and two men who had just left Tesla.

15
00:01:13,582 --> 00:01:22,651
Peter Carlsson had run supply chain at Tesla during the Model S ramp; Paolo Cerruti was a vice president in the same function.

16
00:01:22,651 --> 00:01:27,777
In 2015 they founded SGF Energy in Stockholm, renamed Northvolt in March 2017.

17
00:01:27,777 --> 00:01:31,325
The pitch was clean and, at the time, unanswerable.

18
00:01:31,325 --> 00:01:38,028
Europe's carmakers would soon need hundreds of gigawatt-hours of cells a year, almost all made in Asia.

19
00:01:38,028 --> 00:01:43,548
Northern Sweden had cheap hydro power, land, and a government fond of industrial policy.

20
00:01:43,548 --> 00:01:51,434
Northvolt would build "the world's greenest battery" and give European carmakers a supplier that was not Chinese, Korean or Japanese.

21
00:01:51,434 --> 00:01:55,772
Investors, and Brussels, found this extremely easy to say yes to.

22
00:01:56,172 --> 00:01:58,561
The empire, at its peak.

23
00:01:58,561 --> 00:01:59,995
Headquarters in Stockholm.

24
00:01:59,995 --> 00:02:03,819
Northvolt Labs, research and pilot plant, in Västerås.

25
00:02:03,819 --> 00:02:10,511
Northvolt Ett, the gigafactory, in Skellefteå, two hundred kilometres south of the Arctic Circle.

26
00:02:10,511 --> 00:02:14,335
A joint venture with Volvo Cars in Gothenburg.

27
00:02:14,335 --> 00:02:17,203
Northvolt Dwa, energy-storage assembly, in Gdańsk.

28
00:02:17,203 --> 00:02:23,417
Northvolt Drei, a second gigafactory breaking ground in Heide, Schleswig-Holstein, in March 2024.

29
00:02:23,417 --> 00:02:31,065
Off this map: Northvolt Six, a seven-billion-Canadian-dollar plant planned outside Montreal, and a Californian subsidiary, Cuberg.

30
00:02:31,065 --> 00:02:39,190
Six countries, five factories in various states of existence, and, as of 2023, one shipping commercial cells.

31
00:02:39,590 --> 00:02:40,916
Follow the money.

32
00:02:40,916 --> 00:02:48,871
In 2017 and 2018, small European Investment Bank loans and seed money from Vargas, Vattenfall, ABB and Scania.

33
00:02:48,871 --> 00:03:06,548
In June 2019, the round that made the company: a billion dollars of equity led by Volkswagen and Goldman Sachs, with BMW, AMF, Folksam and IKEA's IMAS Foundation alongside; Volkswagen paid about nine hundred million euros for roughly twenty percent.

34
00:03:06,548 --> 00:03:13,176
In 2020, one point six billion of bank debt and six hundred million of equity.

35
00:03:13,176 --> 00:03:16,270
In 2021, two point seven five billion.

36
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:22,457
Convertibles of one point one and one point two billion in 2022 and 2023.

37
00:03:22,457 --> 00:03:33,947
And in January 2024, five billion dollars of project finance from twenty-three banks plus the EIB and Nordic Investment Bank, billed as Europe's largest green loan.

38
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:38,333
Volkswagen about twenty-one percent, Goldman Sachs funds about nineteen.

39
00:03:38,333 --> 00:03:48,078
Denmark's ATP five point three, the Swedish national AP funds together about three point seven, on five point eight billion kronor invested.

40
00:03:48,078 --> 00:03:53,836
Then a long tail: BMW, Scania, Baillie Gifford, Canada's OMERS, Spotify's Daniel Ek.

41
00:03:53,836 --> 00:04:00,037
Lenders: the EIB, KfW, and export credit agencies from Sweden, Germany, Korea and Japan.

42
00:04:00,037 --> 00:04:10,667
Northvolt told these people in January 2024 that it held over fifty-five billion dollars of supply contracts with BMW, Scania, Volvo Cars and Volkswagen.

43
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:17,311
Nobody, so far as we can tell, asked how many cells had shipped against them.

44
00:04:17,711 --> 00:04:19,933
Ambition, in 2019, was the product.

45
00:04:19,933 --> 00:04:25,117
Ett was designed for sixteen gigawatt-hours, then thirty-two; by 2023 the plan was sixty.

46
00:04:25,117 --> 00:04:31,412
The company hired between one and two hundred people a month, from more than a hundred countries.

47
00:04:31,412 --> 00:04:41,780
Everyone around the table wanted it to be true: Volkswagen needed a non-Asian supplier, Brussels needed a Battery Alliance flagship, Sweden needed an industrial future in the north.

48
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,631
That is not a conspiracy.

49
00:04:43,631 --> 00:04:50,297
It is a market with many buyers and exactly one seller of the thing they wanted to hear.

50
00:04:50,697 --> 00:04:53,184
On paper the sequence is orderly.

51
00:04:53,184 --> 00:04:58,990
Money in, factory up, first cell in December 2021, first delivery in May 2022.

52
00:04:58,990 --> 00:05:12,258
What it leaves out is the ratio of announcements to physical cells: nearly every point on this line is a press release, and only one, May 2022, is a customer receiving product.

53
00:05:12,258 --> 00:05:20,966
The plant, meanwhile, was being built, commissioned and debugged simultaneously, in a town whose previous industrial boom was a gold rush.

54
00:05:21,366 --> 00:05:23,160
A word about the place.

55
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:38,232
Skellefteå is a municipality of about seventy-two thousand on the Gulf of Bothnia, known outside Sweden, if at all, for its ice hockey team and for Boliden, the mining company that began when someone found gold in a bog nearby in 1924.

56
00:05:38,232 --> 00:05:43,256
There is a dry local memory of what happens when outsiders arrive with equipment.

57
00:05:43,256 --> 00:05:56,534
Between 2019 and 2024 the town built housing, schools and a wooden cultural centre the height of a tower block, and the local paper, Norran, began publishing in English because many new readers could not read Swedish.

58
00:05:56,534 --> 00:06:03,353
One can be a battery factory's biggest fan and still notice the fan base growing faster than the output.

59
00:06:03,753 --> 00:06:09,960
The year the story turns, as two bars, one of which you may need to squint at.

60
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:14,707
In 2019 Northvolt said Ett would make sixteen gigawatt-hours a year by 2023.

61
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:26,026
In the first nine months of 2023 it made seventy-nine point eight megawatt-hours, not quite half a percent of the promise, while losing around eleven billion kronor, roughly a billion dollars.

62
00:06:26,026 --> 00:06:32,964
Volume did improve; by early 2025 the company said serial-line output had doubled and yields were up fifty percent.

63
00:06:32,964 --> 00:06:41,362
But when a chairman calls it a marathon, remember that customers were promised the runner in 2023 and were still waiting in 2025.

64
00:06:41,762 --> 00:06:46,192
The post-mortem, from local reporting and a former employee's book, is unglamorous.

65
00:06:46,192 --> 00:06:59,851
Much of the line equipment came from Wuxi Lead and other Chinese suppliers, arrived with Chinese manuals, and broke down often; when it did, staff in the Arctic winter got on video calls with technicians in Jiangsu.

66
00:06:59,851 --> 00:07:00,958
Humidity control failed.

67
00:07:00,958 --> 00:07:06,865
Employees say that at one point about half the output went straight to the defects division.

68
00:07:06,865 --> 00:07:16,462
The in-house cathode plant, central to the "greenest battery" story, could not make material to specification, so from early 2024 Northvolt quietly imported cathode from China.

69
00:07:16,462 --> 00:07:20,523
Several accounts describe bad news from the floor being unwelcome upstairs.

70
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:22,369
None of this is exotic.

71
00:07:22,369 --> 00:07:26,799
It is what a factory looks like when fundraising sets the schedule.

72
00:07:27,199 --> 00:07:33,433
On the evening of 4 November 2023 there was an explosion inside the Skellefteå plant.

73
00:07:33,433 --> 00:07:40,499
A twenty-five-year-old employee from elsewhere in Europe, months into the job, died of his burns weeks later.

74
00:07:40,499 --> 00:07:47,150
In early 2024 four more employees died within months; police found no link to their work.

75
00:07:47,150 --> 00:07:48,812
The explosion is different.

76
00:07:48,812 --> 00:08:00,035
In May 2025 prosecutor Christer Jarlås notified Peter Carlsson, chairman of the Ett subsidiary, that he was suspected of gross negligence resulting in death, alongside several managers.

77
00:08:00,035 --> 00:08:05,854
As of June 2026 the prosecutor intends to charge, deciding no earlier than autumn.

78
00:08:05,854 --> 00:08:11,257
Carlsson has called the accident "incredibly unfortunate and sad" and awaits the investigation.

79
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:14,684
The January 2024 loan was the high-water mark.

80
00:08:14,684 --> 00:08:25,659
On 20 June, BMW cancelled a two-billion-euro cell contract signed in 2020, according to Handelsblatt and Manager Magazin because Northvolt was two years late and scrapping too much product.

81
00:08:25,659 --> 00:08:27,929
The order went to Samsung SDI.

82
00:08:27,929 --> 00:08:30,957
A one point two billion dollar raise failed.

83
00:08:30,957 --> 00:08:37,768
In September Northvolt cut sixteen hundred jobs and reset the target from sixty gigawatt-hours to the original sixteen.

84
00:08:37,768 --> 00:08:41,552
In October Volvo Cars took over the Gothenburg joint venture.

85
00:08:41,552 --> 00:08:45,715
Cash was leaving at about a hundred million dollars a month.

86
00:08:45,715 --> 00:08:54,040
Of two point seven billion euros in public loans announced over the years, only about five hundred and thirty million had arrived.

87
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:57,068
The rest had conditions, now impossible to meet.

88
00:08:57,468 --> 00:09:07,343
On 21 November 2024 Northvolt filed for Chapter 11 in Texas: five point eight billion dollars of debt against thirty million of cash, about a week's runway.

89
00:09:07,343 --> 00:09:11,366
Scania, truck maker and customer, put up a hundred-million-dollar debtor-in-possession loan.

90
00:09:11,366 --> 00:09:17,584
The next day Carlsson resigned as chief executive, saying he was "confident" more capital could be raised.

91
00:09:17,584 --> 00:09:27,459
Goldman Sachs funds wrote their eight hundred and ninety-six million dollar stake to zero; the FT reported it had been marked at four times cost months earlier.

92
00:09:27,459 --> 00:09:28,922
Volkswagen wrote down too.

93
00:09:28,922 --> 00:09:36,969
Deputy prime minister Ebba Busch said the state backed the battery industry but had "no plans to take a stake in Northvolt".

94
00:09:36,969 --> 00:09:38,798
Nobody else stepped forward either.

95
00:09:39,198 --> 00:09:45,662
The creditor list from the Texas filing is a map of who wanted a European battery champion.

96
00:09:45,662 --> 00:09:49,844
Two point seven six billion dollars in a convertible loan vehicle.

97
00:09:49,844 --> 00:09:52,506
Six hundred and seventy million from KfW.

98
00:09:52,506 --> 00:09:55,168
Three hundred and thirty million from Volkswagen.

99
00:09:55,168 --> 00:10:04,293
Around one point seven billion of secured debt on the Skellefteå plant, across the EIB and the German, Korean and Japanese export credit agencies.

100
00:10:04,293 --> 00:10:10,377
Near the bottom, suppliers, including Chinese equipment makers reportedly owed close to half a billion euros.

101
00:10:10,377 --> 00:10:16,841
In Sweden the trustee counts claims of around ninety billion kronor against assets of somewhat over forty.

102
00:10:16,841 --> 00:10:20,263
Unsecured recoveries, when they come, will not be generous.

103
00:10:20,663 --> 00:10:24,734
That is the trustee, a year on, and he has a point.

104
00:10:24,734 --> 00:10:35,928
Swedish bankruptcy is a liquidation, not a reorganisation, and the obvious risk in March 2025 was that a plant twice the size of Arlanda would be switched off and left to the snow.

105
00:10:35,928 --> 00:10:36,945
It was not.

106
00:10:36,945 --> 00:10:46,782
About two hundred staff kept the lines warm through 2025 while Kubu ran a sale; most of the three hundred or so creditors at the first meeting were foreign.

107
00:10:46,782 --> 00:10:52,888
The buyer was not a European carmaker, not a Korean cell maker, and not, notably, a European government.

108
00:10:52,888 --> 00:10:57,637
It was a Silicon Valley startup most people in Skellefteå had never heard of.

109
00:10:58,037 --> 00:11:07,097
Lyten, of San Jose, makes lithium-sulphur cells and had raised some six hundred million dollars, less than Northvolt spent in some quarters.

110
00:11:07,097 --> 00:11:18,627
In August 2025 it agreed to buy the Skellefteå plant, the Västerås labs, the Heide site and the intellectual property, book value near five billion dollars; price undisclosed.

111
00:11:18,627 --> 00:11:20,686
Poland closed in October 2025.

112
00:11:20,686 --> 00:11:31,804
Sweden closed on 27 February 2026, later than planned, with six hundred rehires and a promise of commercial cells, conventional lithium-ion for Scania first, in late 2026.

113
00:11:31,804 --> 00:11:36,746
Recycling followed in March; in July, a memorandum with KfW for Heide.

114
00:11:36,746 --> 00:11:40,864
Quebec wrote off two hundred and seventy million Canadian dollars.

115
00:11:40,864 --> 00:11:46,629
And EdgeConneX is taking part of the site for a gigawatt of data centre.

116
00:11:46,629 --> 00:11:49,923
The hydro power, at least, has a customer.

117
00:11:50,323 --> 00:11:53,179
Now the part we think matters most.

118
00:11:53,179 --> 00:11:58,076
In 2025 CATL alone sold six hundred and sixty-one gigawatt-hours of batteries.

119
00:11:58,076 --> 00:12:02,972
BYD installed close to two hundred, LG Energy Solution over a hundred.

120
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:11,540
Northvolt Ett's nameplate, the number that justified fifteen billion dollars, was sixteen; its output in the critical year, point zero eight.

121
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:18,885
CATL's 2025 net profit was seventy-two billion yuan, around ten billion dollars; its research budget twenty-two billion yuan.

122
00:12:18,885 --> 00:12:30,717
The IEA puts China at over eighty percent of global cell capacity at end-2025 and Europe at six to seven, with European pack prices about thirty-five percent above China's.

123
00:12:30,717 --> 00:12:33,981
This is not a race Northvolt was losing.

124
00:12:33,981 --> 00:12:36,021
It had already been run.

125
00:12:36,421 --> 00:12:37,497
Our position, plainly.

126
00:12:37,497 --> 00:12:41,440
Northvolt did not fail for lack of money, engineers or ambition.

127
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:45,024
It failed because European industrial policy confused capital with capability.

128
00:12:45,024 --> 00:13:00,436
China built its battery industry the other way round: a decade of subsidised domestic demand, dozens of cell makers fighting to the margin, and a home-grown equipment supply chain, so that when a line broke in Ningde the fix was down the road.

129
00:13:00,436 --> 00:13:10,473
Europe skipped that and tried to buy the result with one very large cheque to one very young company, whose plant ran on Chinese machines and Chinese cathode.

130
00:13:10,473 --> 00:13:19,792
CATL, meanwhile, is doing in Europe what Northvolt could not: Erfurt, a hundred gigawatt-hours in Hungary, a Stellantis joint venture in Spain with EU money attached.

131
00:13:19,792 --> 00:13:21,943
Europe will have a battery industry.

132
00:13:21,943 --> 00:13:23,735
Increasingly it will be Chinese-owned.

133
00:13:23,735 --> 00:13:26,244
That was never in the press release.

134
00:13:26,644 --> 00:13:28,884
What this case does not show.

135
00:13:28,884 --> 00:13:38,217
It does not show Europe cannot make cells; the same building is being restarted, one line at a time, on a fraction of the money.

136
00:13:38,217 --> 00:13:53,524
Nor is it, so far, a Wirecard-style fraud: one unit's trustee said in September 2025 that board liability looked unlikely, and the economic-crime allegations in Gunnar Lindstedt's 2026 book remain unconfirmed by the authority itself; Carlsson called them "new to me".

137
00:13:53,524 --> 00:13:57,258
What it shows is a sequencing error at continental scale.

138
00:13:57,258 --> 00:14:00,991
Build the capability, then scale it, then finance the scale.

139
00:14:00,991 --> 00:14:06,218
Northvolt ran that backwards, and the factory has been paying the interest ever since.

140
00:14:06,618 --> 00:14:21,758
Every figure in this video is drawn, where possible, from primary documents: Northvolt's own press releases and Chapter 11 filing, the trustee's statements, Lyten's transaction announcements, and reporting by Reuters, the Financial Times, Bloomberg, Sifted and Norran.

141
00:14:21,758 --> 00:14:26,260
The full numbered list, with links, is in the description below.

142
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:31,579
Where a figure is approximate or contested, we have said so on screen.

143
00:14:31,979 --> 00:14:34,481
That is the Northvolt ledger, so far.

144
00:14:34,481 --> 00:14:39,484
We will update it as Lyten ships cells, Heide closes and the prosecutor decides.

145
00:14:39,484 --> 00:14:54,137
If you found this useful, subscribing helps us make the next one, about a company that did not merely miss its production targets but invented them: Wirecard, Germany's DAX-listed payments firm, and the one point nine billion euros that never existed.

146
00:14:54,137 --> 00:14:56,281
Until then, thank you for watching.

